  "worked_solution": "The series starts with $n=3.$ So the common ratio is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =\\frac{{a}_{4}}{{a}_{3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\frac{3}{5}{(\\frac{3}{2})}^{4+1}}{\\frac{3}{5}{(\\frac{3}{2})}^{3+1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{(\\frac{3}{2})}^{5}}{{(\\frac{3}{2})}^{4}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the series is divergent because $|r|\\ge 1.$",
